    "title": "YOLOv8全功能实战：目标检测、跟踪与姿态估计一体化实现",
    "url": "https://cloud.baidu.com/article/3824464",
    "page_content": "<quark-heading level=\"1\">YOLOv8全功能实战：目标检测、跟踪与姿态估计一体化实现</quark-heading>\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">一、YOLOv8技术架构解析</quark-heading>\\nYOLOv8作为Ultralytics发布的最新实时目标检测框架，在继承前代模型优势的基础上，通过架构创新实现了检测精度与速度的双重突破。其核心改进体现在三个方面：\\n骨干 网络 优化 ：采用CSPNet与ELAN结合的架构设计，通过跨阶段部分连接减少计算冗余。实验表明，在同等参数量下，CSPDarknet53较传统ResNet骨干网络推理速度提升23%，而ELAN模块通过高效特征融合进一步提升了梯度传播效率。\\n解耦头结构创新 ：将分类与回归任务分离设计，配合动态标签分配策略。在COCO数据集上的对比实验显示，解耦头结构使AP值提升1.8个百分点，特别是在小目标检测场景下，\\nmAP@0.5 :0.95指标提升显著。\\n动态锚框机制 ：引入自适应锚框计算，通过K-means++聚类算法生成与数据集分布匹配的锚框。在人体姿态估计任务中，该机制使关键点定位误差（\\nPCKh@0.5 ）降低至4.2%，较固定锚框方案提升15%。\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">二、多任务集成实现方案</quark-heading>\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">2.1 目标检测与跟踪融合</quark-heading>\\n<quark-code>fromultralyticsimportYOLO</quark-code>\\n<quark-code></quark-code>\\n<quark-code># 加载预训练模型</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>model=YOLO('yolov8n-pose.pt')# 姿态估计专用模型</quark-code>\\n<quark-code></quark-code>\\n<quark-code># 配置跟踪参数</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>results=model.track(</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>source='video.mp4',</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>tracking_method='bytetrack',# ByteTrack跟踪算法</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>conf=0.5,</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>iou=0.7,</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>persist=True# 保持跨帧ID</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>)</quark-code>\\n<quark-code></quark-code>\\n<quark-code># 处理跟踪结果</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>forframe_resultinresults:</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>fortrackinframe_result.boxes.data.tolist():</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>print(f\"ID: {int(track[5])}, BBox: {track[:4].tolist()}\")</quark-code>\\n技术要点 ：\\nByteTrack算法通过级联匹配策略，在遮挡场景下ID切换率降低37%\\n跟踪阈值建议：检测置信度>0.5，IOU阈值0.5-0.7\\n实际应用中需配置\\n<quark-code>\\npersist=True\\n</quark-code>\\n保持对象ID\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">2.2 姿态估计关键技术</quark-heading>\\n<quark-code># 姿态估计可视化</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>result=model('person.jpg')</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>forposeinresult:</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>keypoints=pose.keypoints.xy# 获取关键点坐标</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>confidences=pose.keypoints.conf# 置信度</quark-code>\\n<quark-code></quark-code>\\n<quark-code># 绘制骨架连接</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>connections=[</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],# 头部连接</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>[4,5],[5,6],[6,7],# 左臂</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>[8,9],[9,10],[10,11]# 右臂</quark-code>\\n<quark-code>]</quark-code>\\n<quark-code># 实际绘制代码需结合OpenCV实现</quark-code>\\n精度优化策略 ：\\n数据增强组合 ：采用Mosaic+MixUp增强，使关键点定位误差降低12%\\n热图解码优化 ：使用高斯核σ=2.0生成热图，配合OKS（Object Keypoint Similarity）评估指标\\n多尺度测试 ：在测试时采用[640,1280]多尺度输入，AP提升2.1个百分点"
  },
  "122": {
    "title": "YOLOv8 Output Extraction Tutorial | Ultralytics",
    "url": "https://www.ultralytics.com/blog/extracting-outputs-from-ultralytics-yolov8",
    "page_content": "Model Initialization: Initialize the YOLOv8 model appropriately, making sure you choose the right model configuration that suits your specific needs, be it object detection or more complex tasks like pose estimation.\\nRunning Inference: Input your data through the model to perform inference. This process will generate a results object, which is your key to accessing all detection data.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">Understanding the results object #</quark-heading>\\nThe results object in YOLOv8 is a goldmine of information. It contains all the detection data that you need to proceed with your project, including:\\nBounding Boxes: Use\\n<quark-code>\\nresults.boxes\\n</quark-code>\\nto access coordinates of detected objects.\\nMasks and Keypoints: Access segmentation masks and keypoints for pose estimation using\\n<quark-code>\\nresults.masks\\n</quark-code>\\nand\\n<quark-code>\\nresults.keypoints\\n</quark-code>\\nrespectively.\\nClass Probabilities:\\n<quark-code>\\nresults.probs\\n</quark-code>\\nprovides the likelihood of each detected class, useful for filtering detections based on confidence scores.\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">Extracting data for custom use #</quark-heading>\\nTo use these outputs in your applications, follow these steps:\\nConvert Data for Processing: If you’re running your model on a GPU, convert the outputs to CPU format using .cpu() for further manipulation.\\nAccessing Bounding Box Coordinates: Retrieve and manipulate bounding box coordinates directly from the results object. This includes accessing normalized coordinates or specific attributes like width and height.\\nHandling Classifications: Extract top classifications to utilize class IDs and confidence scores effectively."
  },
  "123": {
    "title": "Get Started with YOLOv8: Real-Time Object Detection on Your Laptop - DFRobot",
    "url": "https://www.dfrobot.com/blog-13903.html?srsltid=AfmBOopXUVUv6IcRXXO0TpKldLKWGisZA6UTCBY7qma5l6AgEmmHCIBP",
    "page_content": "<quark-code>\\nPython\\nimport cv2\\nimport time\\nimport torch\\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\\n# load YOLOv8n\\nmodel = YOLO('yolov8n.pt')\\ncap = cv2.VideoCapture(0)\\nif not cap.isOpened():\\n    print(\"error\")\\n    exit()\\nwidth = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_WIDTH))\\nheight = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_HEIGHT))\\nprev_time = 0\\nfps = 0\\nwhile True:\\n    ret, frame = cap.read()\\n    if not ret:\\n        print(\"error\")\\n        break\\n    results = model(frame, device='cpu')\\n    for result in results:\\n        boxes = result.boxes.xyxy.cpu().numpy()\\n        confidences = result.boxes.conf.cpu().numpy()\\n        class_ids = result.boxes.cls.cpu().numpy().astype(int)\\n        for i in range(len(boxes)):\\n            box = boxes[i]\\n            x1, y1, x2, y2 = map(int, box[:4])\\n            confidence = confidences[i]\\n            class_id = class_ids[i]\\n            label = result.names[class_id]\\n            cv2.rectangle(frame, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (0, 255, 0), 2)\\n            cv2.putText(frame, f'{label} {confidence:.2f}', (x1, y1 - 10),\\n                        cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.9, (36, 255, 12), 2)\\n    curr_time = time.time()\\n    fps = 1 / (curr_time - prev_time)\\n    prev_time = curr_time\\n    cv2.putText(frame, f'FPS: {fps:.2f}', (10, 30), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 1, (0, 255, 0), 2)\\n    cv2.imshow('YOLOv8n Real-time', frame)\\n    if cv2.waitKey(1) & 0xFF == ord('q'):\\n        break\\ncap.release()\\ncv2.destroyAllWindows()\\n</quark-code>\\nSave the code as a Python file named 'yolov8ndet.py' and run it.\\npy-3\\n<quark-code>\\nBash\\npython yolov8ndet.py\\n</quark-code>\\nTest the performance using the YOLOv8n model: Running speed is 7.49.\\n<quark-ocr>yolovBn.pt 0:480x640 1person,1chair,2tvs,120.5ms Speed:3.0ms preprocess,120.5ms inference, 1.0ms postprocess per  YOLOv8n Real-time Object Detection image at shape （1，3,480,640) FPS:7.49 0:480x640 1 person，1 chair,1tv,119.8ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess,119.8msinference,3.0ms postprocess per image at shape（1,3,480,640) 0:480x640 1 person,2chairs,2tvs,117.4ms Speed:3.0ms preprocess,117.4ms inference, 2.0ms postprocess per image atshape（1,3,480,640) 0:480x640 1 person,1 chair,1tv,118.6ms Speed:2.0mspreprocess,118.6msinference，2 2.0ms postprocess per berson image at shape （1，3,480,640) chail 0:480x640 1 person,2chairs,120.5ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess,120.5ms inference,2.0ms postprocess per image atshape（1,3,480,640) 0:480x640 1person,1 chair,1 tv,120.1ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess,120.1ms inference,2 2.1ms postprocess per imageatshape（1,3,480,640) chali 0.27 0:480x6401person,2chairs,1tv,119.9ms Speed:2.4mspreprocess,119.9ms inference,2.0ms postprocess per image atshape （1,3,480,640)</quark-ocr></quark-image>\\n<quark-heading level=\"3\">Segment</quark-heading>\\ncode：\\npy-3\\n<quark-code>\\nPython\\nimport cv2\\nimport time\\n# import torch\\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nimport numpy as np\\nmodel = YOLO('yolov8n-seg.pt')\\ncap = cv2.VideoCapture(0)\\nif not cap.isOpened():\\n    print(\"error\")\\n    exit()\\nwidth = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_WIDTH))\\nheight = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_HEIGHT))\\nprev_time = 0\\nfps = 0\\nwhile True:\\n    ret, frame = cap.read()\\n    if not ret:\\n        print(\"error\")\\n        break\\n    results = model(frame, device='cpu')\\n    for result in results:\\n        pil_image = Image.fromarray(results[0].plot()[:, :, ::-1])\\n        frame = np.array(pil_image)\\n        boxes = result.boxes.xyxy.cpu().numpy()\\n        confidences = result.boxes.conf.cpu().numpy()\\n        class_ids = result.boxes.cls.cpu().numpy().astype(int)\\n        for i in range(len(boxes)):\\n            box = boxes[i]\\n            x1, y1, x2, y2 = map(int, box[:4])\\n            confidence = confidences[i]\\n            class_id = class_ids[i]\\n            label = result.names[class_id]\\n    curr_time = time.time()\\n    fps = 1 / (curr_time - prev_time)\\n    prev_time = curr_time\\n    cv2.putText(frame, f'FPS: {fps:.2f}', (10, 30), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 1, (0, 255, 0), 2)\\n    cv2.imshow('YOLOv8n Real-time', frame)\\n    if cv2.waitKey(1) & 0xFF == ord('q'):\\n        break\\ncap.release()\\ncv2.destroyAllWindows()\\n</quark-code>\\nSave the code as a Python file named 'yolov8nseg.py' and run it.\\npy-3\\n<quark-code>\\nBash\\npython yolov8nseg.py\\n</quark-code>\\nTest the performance using the YOLOv8n model: Running speed is 5.07.\\n<quark-ocr>YOLOvBn Real-time Object Detection 口 0:480x640 1wine glass,159.5ms Speed:4.0ms preprocess,159.5ms FPS:5.07 inference,5.0ms postprocess per image at shape（1，3,480,640） 0:480x64θ （no detections), 154.5ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess,154.5ms inference,1.0ms postprocess per image at shape （1,3,480,640） 0:480x640 （no detections),1 161.1ms Speed:1.0ms preprocess,161.1ms inference,1.0ms postprocess per image atshape（1，3,480,640) wineglass0.36 0:480x640 1wine glass,1 159.5ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess,159.5ms inference,4.0ms postprocess per image at shape（1，3,480,640) 0:480x6401bottle,1wine glass,157.4ms Speed:1.4ms preprocess,157.4ms inference, 7.0ms postprocess per image at shape （1,3,480,640) 0:480x640 （no detections),149.1ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess,149.1ms inference，2.0ms postprocess per image at shape（1，3,480,640) 0:480x640 1 wine glass,157.1ms Speed:2.0ms preprocess, 157.1ms inference, 5.0ms postprocess per image at shape 480. 640)</quark-ocr></quark-image>"
