  "124": {
    "title": "Human critical point detection - MaixPy",
    "url": "https://wiki.sipeed.com/maixpy/doc/en/vision/body_key_points.html",
    "page_content": "<quark-heading level=\"2\">1. Introduction #</quark-heading>\\nUsing MaixPy, you can easily detect the coordinates of keypoints on human joints, which can be used for posture detection, such as monitoring sitting posture or providing input for motion-based games.\\nMaixPy implements human pose detection based on YOLOv8-Pose / YOLO11-Pose , capable of detecting\\n<quark-code>\\n17\\n</quark-code>\\nkeypoints on the human body.\\n<quark-ocr>.88 person</quark-ocr>\\n<quark-heading level=\"2\">2. Usage #</quark-heading>\\nYou can easily implement this using the\\n<quark-code>\\nmaix.nn.YOLOv8\\n</quark-code>\\nor\\n<quark-code>\\nmaix.nn.YOLO11\\n</quark-code>\\nclasses in MaixPy:\\n<quark-code>from maix import camera, display, image, nn, app\\ndetector = nn.YOLO11(model=\"/root/models/yolo11n_pose.mud\", dual_buff=True)\\n# detector = nn.YOLOv8(model=\"/root/models/yolov8n_pose.mud\", dual_buff=True)\\ncam = camera.Camera(detector.input_width(), detector.input_height(), detector.input_format())\\ndisp = display.Display()\\nwhile not app.need_exit():\\nimg = cam.read()\\nobjs = detector.detect(img, conf_th=0.5, iou_th=0.45, keypoint_th=0.5)\\nfor obj in objs:\\nimg.draw_rect(obj.x, obj.y, obj.w, obj.h, color=image.COLOR_RED)\\nmsg = f'{detector.labels[obj.class_id]}: {obj.score:.2f}'\\nimg.draw_string(obj.x, obj.y, msg, color=image.COLOR_RED)\\ndetector.draw_pose(img, obj.points, 8 if detector.input_width() &gt; 480 else 4, image.COLOR_RED)\\ndisp.show(img)\\n</quark-code>\\nCopy\\nYou can also find the code in the MaixPy/examples/vision directory.\\nSince\\n<quark-code>\\nYOLOv8-Pose\\n</quark-code>\\nis used here, the\\n<quark-code>\\nYOLOv8\\n</quark-code>\\nclass is also used, with the only difference being the model file compared to\\n<quark-code>\\nYOLOv8\\n</quark-code>\\nobject detection. The same applies to\\n<quark-code>\\nYOLO11\\n</quark-code>\\n. The\\n<quark-code>\\ndetect\\n</quark-code>\\nfunction returns an additional\\n<quark-code>\\npoints\\n</quark-code>\\nvalue, which is a list of\\n<quark-code>\\nint\\n</quark-code>\\ncontaining\\n<quark-code>\\n17\\n</quark-code>\\nkeypoints. The points are arranged in order; for example, the first value is the x-coordinate of the nose, the second value is the y-coordinate of the nose, and so on:\\n<quark-code>1. Nose\\n2. Left Eye\\n3. Right Eye\\n4. Left Ear\\n5. Right Ear\\n6. Left Shoulder\\n7. Right Shoulder\\n8. Left Elbow\\n9. Right Elbow\\n10. Left Wrist\\n11. Right Wrist\\n12. Left Hip\\n"
  },
  "125": {
    "title": "自动化生产线搬运机械手控制系统的设计研究 - AMiner",
    "url": "https://www.aminer.org/pub/604b3e926f90b7f6cac97c41/design-research-of-robot-control-system-for-automatic-production-line",
    "page_content": "2.2 Control Requirements for the Robotic Arm X, Y, Z directional motion control\\nVariable frequency speed regulation\\nAutomatic cyclic operation and manual operation\\nPrecise positioning and interlock function\\nEnd effector suction cup airtightness\\n3. Pneumatic Circuit Design\\n3.1 Basic Components of the Pneumatic Circuit Air source device, medium, actuating elements, control elements, auxiliary parts\\nPneumatic schematic of the robotic arm's end\\nSequence table for solenoid valve actions\\n3.2 Selection of Electrical Components Air compressor, solenoid directional valve, suction cup, throttle valve, servo motor, motor driver, motor reducer\\n3.3 Calculation of the Suction Force of the Robotic Arm's End Effector Formula for calculating the diameter of the suction cup\\nCalculation of vacuum degree for horizontal stacking adsorption\\n4. Design of the Robotic Arm Control System\\n4.1 Hardware Composition of the System Main controller PLC and external input/output devices\\nIntroduction to PLC functions\\nInput devices: Sensors, control buttons, control panel, touch screen\\nOutput devices: Solenoid valves, frequency converters, relays, loads\\n4.2 PLC Programming Two control modes: manual switch control and touch screen control\\nPLC I/O port allocation\\nCommand sending process under touch screen control\\nFunctional flowchart of the robotic arm\\n4.3 Control Model of the Servo Motor Physical model of the servo motor\\nControl equations for the servo motor\\nTransfer function of the servo motor\\n5. Touch Screen Interface Establishment and Prototype Experiment\\n5.1 Establishing the Touch Screen Interface MCGS touch screen as a monitoring device\\nEstablishing the relationship between the robotic arm variables and PLC variables\\nSystem online interface monitoring diagram\\n5.2 Simulation Results and Analysis Setting different PID parameters for the motor driver\\nTesting the operational status of the robotic arm\\nMatlab simulation experiment results\\nStep response graph under PID control\\nAdvantages of PID control method\\n6. Conclusion\\nThis paper designs a new type of automated handling stacking robotic arm and control system\\nIntroduces the structure of the robotic arm, pneumatic circuit, motor control, system hardware composition, and PLC I/O allocation\\nEstablishes a control motor model and determines the optimal control parameters through Matlab simulation\\nExperimental results show that the PID control method has superior performance, meeting the design requirements"
  },
  "126": {
    "title": "一文看懂工业机器人末端执行器！不同 “机械手” 分别解决工厂哪些难题- · 科普中国网",
    "url": "https://www.kepuchina.cn/article/articleinfo?ar_id=728901&business_type=100&classify=0",
    "page_content": "我们常看到机械臂灵活抓取零件、焊接车架、搬运纸箱，但真正和工件接触、完成实操工作的，是机械臂最前端的末端执行器，也被大家称作机器人的 “手”。同一台工业机械臂，只需要更换不同末端工具，就能适配十几道生产工序。本文搭配实景对比图解，通俗拆解各类末端执行器结构、工作原理与适用场景，看懂它们如何替代人工、破解制造业各类生产痛点。\\n<quark-ocr>末端执行器：机器人的万能手掌 同一台机械臂，更换不同工具就能完成抓取、焊接、打磨、搬运 夹取 气动夹爪 吸附 焊接 焊接 打磨</quark-ocr>\\n一、 气动机械夹爪 ：制造业最通用的刚性机械手\\n<quark-ocr>工业器人气动机械夹爪 开合手指 防滑耐磨垫片 调节扒程 气动夹爪：稳定夹持小件 气缸驱动：控制开合力度 双指夹爪 防滑垫片：保护工件表面 调节行程旋爪 三指定心夹爪 适合：金属零件、塑料外壳、五金小件装配</quark-ocr>\\n1.基础结构：气缸驱动模块、开合手指、防滑耐磨垫片、调节行程旋钮\\n2.工作原理：压缩空气通入气缸，推动夹爪手指同步开合，依靠机械夹持力固定工件，可手动调节夹持力度与开合范围。\\n3.解决什么生产问题 适用于金属零件、塑料外壳、五金小件抓取装配。人工长时间拿取小件易手部劳损，夹爪力度恒定，24 小时重复作业不疲劳； 定心三指夹爪 可精准居中圆形工件，杜绝人工摆放偏移，降低装配次品率。\\n二、 真空吸盘夹具 ：轻薄板材、箱体专用吸附工具\\n<quark-ocr>工业机器人真空吸盘夹具 真空吸盘： 吸附平整工件 真空发生器 负压原理：牢牢贴合表面 分流管路 缓冲附震震 无夹痕：保护玻璃与板材 支架架 适合： 纸箱码垛、玻璃搬运、薄板上下料</quark-ocr>\\n1.基础结构： 真空发生器 、硅胶吸盘、分流管路、缓冲减震支架\\n2.工作原理：发生器抽出吸盘内部空气形成负压，依靠大气压力牢牢吸附平整光滑工件，断电断气后自动泄压松开工件。\\n3.解决什么生产问题 纸箱、光伏玻璃、木板、金属薄板质地轻薄，夹爪夹持容易压伤、刮花表面。真空吸盘无刚性挤压，完整保护工件外观；码垛场景中单次可吸附多件物料，搬运效率远超人工。\\n三、 焊接专用执行器 ：焊枪一体式机器人作业头"
  },
  "127": {
    "title": "Towards intelligent object handling: an advanced end-effector for integrated bin-picking and assembly of electrical components | The International Journal of Advanced Manufacturing Technology | Springer Nature Link",
    "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00170-026-17451-9",
    "page_content": "17 . The linear motors responsible for the lateral motion of the suction cup, equipped with encoders for precise feedback, operate via a Controller Area Network (CAN) interface. An MCP2515 CAN bus module interfaces with the microcontroller through an SPI protocol, controlling the two motors. A custom driver has been developed to manage continuous position control, homing routines, and feedback monitoring, providing real-time data on metrics such as current consumption, velocity, position, and error codes. The end-effector is integrated in MoveIt and device’s kinematics can be simulated in both RViz and Gazebo.\\nFig. 17\\nIn-house control API & ROS visualizer\\nFull size image\\nThis work presented the design, development, and evaluation of a multifunctional robotic end-effector tailored for the automated bin-picking and assembly of electrical components onto DIN rails. The proposed solution addresses key limitations of conventional robotic grippers by combining both vacuum-based and parallel grasping mechanisms, enabling in-hand manipulation without the necessity of regrasp stations or additional tooling. The end-effector’s performance was validated through a case study involving the assembly of an elevator control panel, both in a simulated environment and in a real industrial robotic cell. Experimental results demonstrated the device’s capability to handle a diverse range of electrical components with variations in shape, size, and weight, while successfully executing both bin-picking and force-controlled insertion tasks."
  },
  "128": {
